		<id>http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4367&amp;p=32983#p32983</id>
		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4367&amp;p=32983#p32983"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Probable bug in OpenGD77]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4367&amp;p=32983#p32983"><![CDATA[
Alex DL4LEX has done extensive work on SMS, and AFIK was able to receive SMS and possibly send SMS. But the SMS protocol is proprietary and possibly could not be fully implemented in firmware.<br><br>We did release a version where hotspot mode could pass / send / receive SMS and AFIK this functionality worked OK.<br>However we had to withdraw that version, because some of the changes somehow stopped normal operation of voice use for some people.<br>We may add this functionality again when the bugs have been fixed, but currently we have higher priority things to work on, and very limited time in our lives to spend on this project<br><br>Its possible when the official firmware sends and receives SMS that it configures the C6000 differently, but this firmware was written to work for voice traffic.<br><br><br>I don't know if Alex DL4LEX is still working on SMS support or not. You would need to contact him directly. But from what I understand he thinks its not practical to support SMS.<br><br><br>There is nothing to stop you modifying the firmware in any way to support your own specific usage, but we will not be modifying the firmware which in any way reduces its normal functionality, for voice traffic under a wide variety of conditions.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Mon Sep 16, 2024 9:57 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
		<entry>
		<author><name><![CDATA[G4EML]]></name></author>
		<updated>2024-09-16T21:13:18</updated>

		<published>2024-09-16T21:13:18</published>
		<id>http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4367&amp;p=32981#p32981</id>
		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4367&amp;p=32981#p32981"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Probable bug in OpenGD77]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4367&amp;p=32981#p32981"><![CDATA[
It is a hardware problem. We have proved that the HRC6000 is not good at decoding the signal when operating in AF mode. <br><br>There are many settings for the AT1846S and the HRC6000. Many are not documented and we don't know what they do. There may be other settings that would affect reception but finding them would be guesswork. <br><br>As far as we know the manufacturers calibration table does not contain any settings which would affect reception. We are already using all of the parameters that are relevant to the new firmware.<br><br>Adding SMS needs a much better knowledge of the protocol. It is not well documented and parts of it are proprietary to Motorola. It is error tolerant so unlikely to be connected to your issue.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Mon Sep 16, 2024 9:13 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
