		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4367&amp;p=32974#p32974"><![CDATA[
Yes I know it doesn't work, it's because I explained it. With the volume to 0xFF there are some errors on the 0s and 1s in the last bytes. With the volume to 0xCF there are no more errors on the 0s but a lot of errors with the 1s, even in the first bytes.<br><br>You told me that it is impossible for there to be errors with the 1s and not with the 0s.<br><br><em class="text-italics">"The data you posted does not make sense. Why would 0's be 100% correct, and the Silence frame also be OK, but sending all 1's have very high BER"</em><br><br>Ok it's impossible but I see it.<br><br>And I have explained several times that the data is modified before the FEC. The FEC is added after the modified data.<br><br>This shows that it is indeed a software problem with the configuration in reception in opengd77 and not a hardware problem.<br>But apart from the volume, is there anything else that can be modified in the AT1846S.c file or elsewhere, that's what I was asking before:<br><em class="text-italics">Are there any other parameters (other than the internal volume) that could be set in opengd77? Is there any data that manages these parameters for each radio that can be extracted from the radio (such as calibration data)?</em><br><br>Last question, about SMS: no one has been able to reliably send and receive SMS with opengd77: for some it works, for others it doesn't. Is the bug I found: loss of some bits at the reception, could it be related to the problem of SMS?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4783">JP7NJT</a> — Mon Sep 16, 2024 5:46 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
