		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4367&amp;p=32912#p32912"><![CDATA[
Another update on the effects of reducing the AF gain.<br><br>During testing several people reported that reducing the AF  gain completely stops the firmware working with their hotspot.<br><br>So it is not going to be possible to release a version with lower gain setting.<br><br>@JP7NJT, your use-case is not the normal use-case for this firmware. So if it does not work for your purpose, you will need to modify it to suit your own needs.<br><br>It is unlikely that we would add a calibration setting for this, as almost no one would use it. Especially as AFIK there is no way to determine the Rx BER, without sending test patterns from another radio<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Sep 13, 2024 9:48 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
